Observed local implementation subsets using gsea_res$pvalue <= pvalueCutoff without an NA guard.
This base-R subset turns untestable rows into all-NA rows and filters nominal P, not adjusted P.

Interpretation limits
These CSVs are nominal-P-filtered exports, not the full tested-pathway inventory.
Do not use exported nrow as the number of significant or testable pathways.
All-NA rows are not nonsignificant pathways; their identifiers are lost in the export.
The finite top-ranked rows still require an explicit prespecified FDR threshold.
No input, result, dependency or repository file was modified by this QC script.
